    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the measurement, and it is right: the trace (EV-GPS-02839) records 24.6 km against the booked optimal of 20.0 km (EV-TRIP-02839), an excess of 4.6 km and 23.0%, so both POL-RD-01 gates (over 0.8 km and over 20%) are passed and a deviation is established on this trip's own evidence. The live question is what excuses it.\n\nThe KPE closure advisory (EV-ADVIS-02839-01) excuses the whole of it under POL-RD-03. It is an LTA DataMall HIGH-severity closure on the Kallang-Paya Lebar Expressway towards ECP after Defu Flyover, active 2026-08-21 17:53:08 to 19:20:08, which covers the trace window of 18:23:08 to 18:55:08; the record marks it as intersecting the route, so the optimal route traverses the affected segment; and the trace never enters the advisory's area (0 fixes inside, closest approach 1350.67 m), which is what a route that leaves the corridor before the affected segment and rejoins it after looks like - the vehicle cannot have driven the closed segment and still reached the same drop-off. The shortest lawful alternative is 23.0 km against the 20.0 km booked optimal, and the justified excess is min(4.6, 1.30 x (23.0 - 20.0) + 1.0 = 4.9) = 4.6 km, so the entire excess is exonerated and nothing remains to refund on distance or time. Because POL-RD-03 fully excuses the deviation, POL-RD-02 does not run at all (it applies only where no exculpatory clause fully excuses it). That is why the rider's $7.85 recomputation against the booked optimal is set aside (it assumes the closure did not count) and the driver's $2.70 closure-branch recomputation is set aside too (it re-prices the adjusted route at a scaled 33.2 minutes rather than the 32.0 minutes actually driven).\n\nThe one line the rider does recover is the ERP. The ECP Fort Rd eastbound charge of $3.00 (EV-FARE-02839) lies off the booked optimal route (on_optimal_route false; optimal-route ERP $0.00), and the rider did not cause the closure either, so under POL-RD-09(2) it is refunded as a standalone pass-through correction, well inside the $12.00 cap. It is not added on top of any POL-RD-02 refund, because there is none (POL-RD-09(1)). The gantry is a real crossing and not a phantom line: the nearest trace fix is 59.12 m away at 18:39:08, inside the 250 m match radius (EV-FARE-02839, EV-GPS-02839), so the 'a gantry I would never have passed' part of the claim fails and no billing-integrity referral arises under POL-RD-09(4).\n\nNo repeat-deviation uplift or referral: the excess is 23.0% against the 50% material threshold and 4.6 km against the 8.0 km threshold, and the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 197 completed trips in 90 days (EV-DPROF-02839), below both POL-RD-06 tests. No driver compensation is due: the billed distance (24.6 km) equals the trace distance, so there is no unbilled shortfall under POL-RD-04. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02839) is empty, no endpoint was amended, the vehicle type is RYDE_X and the fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 do not apply. Nothing on either profile other than the two counters POL-RD-06 and POL-RD-08 name was used as a ground (POL-GEN-01).\n\nNo escalation is required: the trace is clean (193 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, maximum gap 0 s), the trip identifiers match across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown, the advisory relied on is present and covers the trip window, and every fare line is matched to the trace.\n\nOutcome: of the $7.00 contested, $3.00 is refunded - the off-route ERP only. The distance and time charges stand (charged_total $35.01 less the $3.00 ERP line), and the refund is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically under POL-GEN-05. Both parties may appeal once under POL-GEN-04.",
